      "target": "../sections/sec-018-33-preventing-monitoring-and-managing-amphoteric.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "deoxycholate toxicity\nManaging toxicity (2022 good practice principles)\nInfusion-related toxicity and side-effects from amphotericin B therapy are barriers to optimal induction treatment, \nespecially in low- and middle-income countries.\n• Safe administration of amphotericin B should be given priority and may require referral to a centre with access to the \nrecommended package of preventing, monitoring and managing toxicity.\n•\t Liposomal amphotericin B has fewer risks of drug toxicity than amphotericin B deoxycholate and requires a less \nintensive package for preventing, monitoring and managing",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Sets out good practice principles for preventing, monitoring and managing amphotericin B toxicity, such as hypokalaemia, nephrotoxicity and anaemia. It describes pre-hydration, electrolyte supplementation and laboratory monitoring, and how to weigh continuing deoxycholate treatment when severe anaemia develops.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
