      "pageEnd": 30,
      "target": "../sections/sec-019-34-drug-interactions.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Drug interactions in the context of concurrent use of amphotericin, flucytosine and fluconazole \nalongside ART regimens have not been well documented (45).\nHowever, individuals receiving tenofovir disoproxil fumarate (TDF)–based regimens who are \nreceiving amphotericin or recently received amphotericin B preparations should be closely \nmonitored for nephrotoxicity. Liposomal preparations of amphotericin B are considered to be \nsafer (46) than deoxycholate but would still require close follow-up. The dose of TDF should be \nadjusted for renal function.\nFlucytosine, following its absorption and m",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes possible interactions between antifungal drugs and ART, advising kidney monitoring and dose adjustment of tenofovir with amphotericin and haematological monitoring with flucytosine.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
