    {
      "id": "library/10665-357088/blocks/prose-sec-020",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Consolidation and maintenance treatment",
      "pageStart": 30,
      "pageEnd": 30,
      "target": "../sections/sec-020-35-consolidation-and-maintenance-treatment.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "The 2018 WHO recommendations for consolidation and maintenance treatment for cryptococcal \ndisease remain unchanged (16).\nConsolidation (2018 recommendation)\nRecommendation  \nFluconazole (800 mg daily for adults, 6–12 mg/kg per day for children and adolescents up to a maximum of 800 mg \ndaily) is recommended for the consolidation phase (for eight weeks following the induction phase).  \nStrong recommendation; low-certainty evidence\nMaintenance (2018 recommendation)\nFluconazole (200 mg daily for adults, 6 mg/kg per day for adolescents and children) is recommended for the \nmaintenance phase until",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Restates the unchanged 2018 recommendations for fluconazole doses in the consolidation phase and in maintenance therapy until immune reconstitution.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-11"
      }
