    {
      "id": "library/10665-357088/blocks/prose-sec-024",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Timing of ART initiation",
      "pageStart": 32,
      "pageEnd": 32,
      "target": "../sections/sec-024-39-timing-of-art-initiation.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Timing of ART (2018 recommendations)\nImmediate ART initiation is not recommended among adults, adolescents and children living with HIV who have \ncryptococcal meningitis because of the risk of increased mortality and should be deferred 4–6 weeks from the initiation \nof antifungal treatment.  \nStrong recommendation; low-certainty evidence for adults and very-low-certainty evidence for children and adolescents",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Restates the 2018 recommendation that ART be deferred 4–6 weeks after starting antifungal treatment for cryptococcal meningitis because immediate ART raises mortality.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-11"
      }
