    {
      "id": "library/10665-357088/blocks/prose-sec-029",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Cryptococcal immune reconstitution inflammatory syndrome",
      "pageStart": 35,
      "pageEnd": 36,
      "target": "../sections/sec-029-3102-cryptococcal-immune-reconstitution-inflamma.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Paradoxical cryptococcal immune reconstitution inflammatory syndrome is associated \nwith high mortality (13). The median time to onset in reported cohort studies is typically \n3–12 weeks after initiating ART (67). Raised intracranial pressure is a common feature of \ncryptococcal immune reconstitution inflammatory syndrome and an important contributor to \nhigh mortality (68). Multiple repeat lumbar puncture may be necessary. Optimizing antifungal \ntherapy and reinduction with an amphotericin B–based regimen is important if suboptimal \nantifungal treatment is considered to contribute to developi",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes cryptococcal immune reconstitution inflammatory syndrome after starting ART and lists management steps: continue ART, control intracranial pressure, optimize antifungals and consider short-course steroids for life-threatening deterioration.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-11"
      }
