      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "\u0007\u0007RESEARCH NEEDS",
      "pageStart": 38,
      "pageEnd": 39,
      "target": "../sections/sec-031-5-research-needs.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Further research is needed to assess the value of cryptococcal antigen screening at CD4 cell \ncount thresholds between 100 and 200 cells/mm3, which has been suggested to save costs if \ncarried out in inpatient settings.\nHigh cryptococcal antigen titres (>160) in blood have been found to predict subclinical \nmeningitis. It has been suggested that blood titres could be used to predict meningitis in \nsettings in which lumbar puncture cannot be performed or in which providing lumbar puncture \nfor everyone screening cryptococcal antigen–positive is operationally challenging; the \nfeasibility of thi",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Lists research needs, such as screening at CD4 counts of 100–200, using blood antigen titres to predict meningitis, managing relapse and integrating screening into advanced HIV care packages.",
