      "target": "../sections/sec-034-annex-1-process-for-developing-the-guidelines.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "THE GUIDELINES\nWHO first published a rapid advice document on the diagnosis, prevention and management of \ncryptococcal disease in December 2011. \nIn 2018, WHO published guidelines in response to new evidence relating to preventing, screening \nand treating cryptococcal disease. In 2021, new evidence on induction therapy was published \nthat triggered a review of the evidence and a WHO guideline development process. A Guideline \nDevelopment Group meeting was held in February 2022 to review the evidence and formulate a \nrecommendation on the preferred induction regimen for treating people with cr",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Annex 1 of the WHO cryptococcal disease guidelines outlines how they were developed, from the 2011 rapid advice and 2018 guidelines to a February 2022 Guideline Development Group meeting prompted by new evidence on induction therapy. It explains the use of GRADE to rate evidence certainty and set recommendation strength, and how evidence was summarized and presented. It also describes how declarations of interest from the Guideline Development Group and External Review Group were reviewed and managed.",
