    {
      "id": "library/10665-357088/blocks/prose-sec-041",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Discussion",
      "pageStart": 57,
      "pageEnd": 57,
      "target": "../sections/sec-041-discussion.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "This updated review identified one study of 844 participants comparing a novel induction strategy \nfor treating people with a first episode of HIV-associated cryptococcal meningitis. In the single \nstudy included in this systematic review, single high-dose (10 mg/kg) liposomal amphotericin B with \nflucytosine and fluconazole was non-inferior to the WHO-recommended standard-of-care induction \ntherapy for HIV-associated cryptococcal meningitis, with significantly fewer adverse events. Based \non low-certainty evidence from one study, mortality within 10 weeks may be lower with single-\ndose liposo",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Discusses the findings, concluding that single high-dose liposomal amphotericin B with flucytosine and fluconazole was non-inferior to standard induction therapy with fewer adverse events. It notes the limitation of relying on one trial and differences between trial and routine settings, and states that WHO issued updated guidelines in March 2022 recommending the regimen, calling for wider access to the drugs.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
